KernelGuard is licensed per directory (see REUSE.toml for the exact mapping):

  linux/                GPL-2.0-only   (the kernel module must be GPL-compatible;
                                        linux/include/kernelguard_uapi.h adds the
                                        Linux-syscall-note exception so user space
                                        may include it)
  windows/              MIT
  build.py, build.sh,
  build.cmd, kgbuild/   MIT
  *.md, docs, CI files  MIT

The full texts are in LICENSES/:

  LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt
  LICENSES/Linux-syscall-note.txt
  LICENSES/MIT.txt

Each source file that carries an "SPDX-License-Identifier:" line is governed by
that line. Everything else is covered by the REUSE.toml mapping.
